# Sidecar direct dependencies. Locked into sidecar/requirements.lock (full transitive
# closure + sha256 hashes) via the script in the lock header: resolve the closure
# from a working sidecar env, fetch digests from the PyPI JSON API.
# (pip-compile does not finish here: torch backtracking over the CPU+PyPI indexes
# hangs; do not "fix" this by unpinning.)
# Policy: exact `==` pins here. No lower-bound flexibility — a silent
# torch / sentence-transformers / numpy drift previously shipped a materially different
# runtime with no CI signal. Bump pins deliberately, recompile, then re-verify.
#
# Torch CPU note: on Linux the default PyPI torch wheel bundles CUDA (~GBs, slow CI).
# The CPU index below makes the small CPU-only wheel available; CI installs torch from
# it first (pip then sees the pin as satisfied and skips the CUDA wheel).
--extra-index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu

